{
 "name": "ICM | Calculate Credits",
 "note": "EVERY CASE IS A DRY RUN. A suite that writes pay is a suite nobody can run twice, and the write path is the one thing here whose side effects reach a bank account - it is proved by hand (run 6aa2af693c7f7b6b91132e7c, 6 credits landed, run marked Succeeded) and deliberately not by this file. What the suite pins is the FOLD: which lane won, whether the row's own split was read, that a negative amount survives, and that each refusal keeps its own name. The counts below are measured against the seeded test bed AND the pre-existing SEP-2026 rows on tool; re-seeding does not change them, but somebody adding a September transaction will, and that is a true failure rather than a flaky one. The index-based checks below are only legitimate because n_Calc SORTS its output (deal, then person, then the direct credit before the rolled copies); fetch order is promised by nothing. The last six cases run against TEST-NA-JUL-2026, a slice of the customer's real 2,917-row Salesforce export - see records/na-sample-jul2026.json for what each order proves and why Total Amount is not a per-order base.",
